# Creating Cursor rules

This Cursor rule supplements the repository AGENTS.md instructions. It may add scoped requirements but may not weaken root security invariants.

**Authority:** root [`AGENTS.md`](../../AGENTS.md) · [`docs/AGENTS.md`](../../docs/AGENTS.md)

Use this file when adding or revising `.cursor/rules/*.mdc`. Nested and root `AGENTS.md` remain authoritative; `.mdc` files reinforce only.

---

## Frontmatter (required)

Every rule file must start with YAML frontmatter that includes all three fields:

| Field | Purpose |
| ----- | ------- |
| `description` | Short, searchable summary of when the rule applies |
| `globs` | File patterns that auto-attach the rule (string or YAML array) |
| `alwaysApply` | `true` only for genuinely universal rules; otherwise `false` |

```yaml
---
description: Clear one-line purpose
globs: path/to/**/*
alwaysApply: false
---
```

Multi-pattern globs prefer a YAML array:

```yaml
globs: ["packages/core/**/*", "apps/web/src/workers/**/*"]
```

When `alwaysApply: true`, omit `globs` (they are ignored). Do not invent undocumented frontmatter keys.

---

## Writing standards

- Keep rules short and actionable — prefer under ~50 lines of body.
- Prefer **negative constraints** (what NOT to do) over vague aspirations.
- Avoid fluffy language ("be thoughtful", "try to", "generally prefer excellence").
- One concern per file; link to the matching root/nested `AGENTS.md` instead of copying full policy.
- Never put critical security policy only in `.mdc` — reinforce root `AGENTS.md`.
- Include this authority line in every new rule:

> This Cursor rule supplements the repository AGENTS.md instructions. It may add scoped requirements but may not weaken root security invariants.

---

## Pattern anchors (required for coding-pattern rules)

When the rule teaches a specific coding pattern, include at least one **BAD** and one **GOOD** snippet.

### BAD — vague, no anchors, weak frontmatter

```markdown
---
description: Write nice React
alwaysApply: true
---

Try to make components clean and reusable when possible.
```

### GOOD — scoped, negative constraints, BAD/GOOD anchors

````markdown
---
description: Web components must reuse shadcn primitives
globs: apps/web/src/components/**/*
alwaysApply: false
---

# UI primitives

This Cursor rule supplements the repository AGENTS.md instructions. It may add scoped requirements but may not weaken root security invariants.

- Do not introduce a new UI library.
- Do not hand-roll buttons/inputs when `components/ui` already provides them.

### BAD

```tsx
export function PrimaryButton(props: { label: string }) {
  return <button className="rounded bg-blue-500 px-3 py-2">{props.label}</button>;
}
```

### GOOD

```tsx
import { Button } from "@/components/ui/button";

export function PrimaryButton(props: { label: string }) {
  return <Button>{props.label}</Button>;
}
```
````

---

## Body format

Use clear Markdown structure for scanability:

1. `#` title matching the concern
2. Authority / AGENTS link (one short paragraph)
3. `##` sections with bullet lists for constraints
4. `### BAD` / `### GOOD` for pattern rules
5. No essay prose; no duplicated full operating protocol or report templates
